  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the Mekong Australia Partnership (MAP), Australia provides regional and short-term courses, institutional twinning arrangements and long-term Masters-level scholarships, to improve institutional and human capacity. In 2022, through MAP funding, the Australian Competition and Consumer Commission (ACCC) delivered the &#x2018;Thailand-Australia Competition Law Implementation Program&#x2019;, which provided technical assistance in support of effective competition law implementation in Thailand. Experts from ACCC visited Bangkok to conduct in-person activities with the Trade Competition Commission of Thailand (TCCT), including a two-day Merger Hypothetical Workshop. Participants rated the workshop&#x2019;s quality and relevance as HIGH and reported that they had improved their knowledge and skills.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the Mekong-Australia Partnership, the Australian Competition and Consumer Commission (ACCC) implemented the second phase of the &#x2018;Thailand-Australia Competition Law Implementation Program&#x2019;. This program provided targeted and practical technical assistance to the Thailand Trade Competition Commission of Thailand (TCCT) in support of effective competition law implementation. In 2024, the investment delivered capacity building activities, including data mentoring and workshops on incorporating economic analysis into competition investigations. This cooperation contributed to the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding between the ACCC and TCCT for continued collaboration on reforms to Thai competition law.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening leadership</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the Mekong-Australia Partnership, the University of Queensland delivered two regional masterclasses in 2024, building the capacity of 42 emerging leaders from Cambodia, Laos, Thailand and Vietnam. The regional masterclass on &#x2018;Responding to the Climate Change Challenge&#x2019; focused on critical issues related to impact of climate change in the Mekong subregion, incorporating Australian and regional cases studies. In a post-masterclass survey, all participants agreed that the masterclass was relevant and applicable to their work. The masterclass on &#x2018;Cooperation and Leadership for Sustainable Development in the Mekong&#x2019; was designed to share Australian expertise on practical aspects of sustainable development and regional collaboration, particularly on shared transboundary issues such as sustainable tourism and water management. The design and delivery of the MAP masterclasses promoted regional leadership and fostered knowledge exchange among participants, including after the course. The participants had their knowledge of sustainable development tested in an assessment taken before and after the masterclass. The group demonstrated significant improvement after the masterclass, with an average test improvement of 26 per cent.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
